       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB174FIED.
      *> kb/Work PB174 - THE OTHER ARM OF THE SAME DISPATCH. THE
      *> COMPANION GOLDEN pb174_float_item_endianness PINS AN ITEM
      *> HIGH-ORDER-LEFT BEATING AN OPTIONS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT; THIS ONE
      *> PINS THE CONVERSE, WHICH A ONE-DIRECTION TEST WOULD LET A
      *> BACKWARDS MERGE PASS. THERE IS NO OPTIONS PARAGRAPH HERE, SO
      *> 11.9.8.3 SR1 GOVERNS: "WHEN THE FLOAT-BINARY CLAUSE IS NOT
      *> SPECIFIED, THE IMPLEMENTOR SHALL SPECIFY WHETHER THE
      *> HIGH-ORDER-LEFT PHRASE OR THE HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT PHRASE IS
      *> IMPLIED" - COBOL.NET DOCUMENTS HIGH-ORDER-LEFT (CONFORMANCE
      *> ANNEX A.1 ITEM 48), SO THE IMPLIED PHRASE IS BIG-ENDIAN AND
      *> THE ITEM'S OWN HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT MUST OVERRIDE IT.
      *>
      *> EXPECTED VALUES COMPUTED FROM 60559:2020 3.4 + 13.18.60.4
      *> GR19a/b, NOT FROM A RUN. BINARY32 1.5 = 0x3FC00000;
      *> BINARY64 -2.25 = 0xC002000000000000 (GR15).
      *>   B32-R  ITEM SAYS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT -> LITTLE -> 00 00 C0 3F
      *>   B32-D  ITEM SAYS NOTHING -> IMPLIED LEFT -> 3F C0 00 00
      *>   B64-R  ITEM SAYS HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT -> LITTLE -> 00 x6 02 C0
      *> FUNCTION ORD IS BYTE+1, SO ORD 0x3F = 64, ORD 0x00 = 1,
      *> ORD 0x02 = 3, ORD 0xC0 = 193.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 GH.
          05 B32-R USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32 HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT VALUE 1.5.
          05 B32-D USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-32 VALUE 1.5.
          05 B64-R USAGE FLOAT-BINARY-64 HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT VALUE -2.25.
       01 XH PIC X(16).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
           MOVE GH TO XH
      *> BYTES 1-4: THE ITEM'S HIGH-ORDER-RIGHT BEATS THE IMPLIED
      *> HIGH-ORDER-LEFT -> 00 00 C0 3F.
           DISPLAY "R=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(4:1)) "]"
      *> BYTES 5-8: NO PHRASE -> SR1'S DOCUMENTED DEFAULT, BIG-ENDIAN.
           DISPLAY "D=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(5:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(8:1)) "]"
      *> BYTES 9-16: BINARY64 -2.25 LITTLE-ENDIAN -> LAST TWO 02 C0.
           DISPLAY "W=[" FUNCTION ORD(XH(9:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(XH(15:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(XH(16:1)) "]"
           DISPLAY "V=[" B32-R " " B32-D " " B64-R "]"
           STOP RUN.
